course: dictionary
lesson: 14821
title: A whining, complaining voice
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words describe how a person sounds, not just what they say. Querulous is one of these. It means complaining in a whining, annoyed voice. «The querulous old man grumbled that the soup was cold, the bus was late, and the sun was too bright.» He complains about everything, so querulous is describing his voice and his mood.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Grumbled, complained and too bright all show that something is bothering him. A whining voice is high, drawn-out and fed up. So when you read querulous, ask: is this person complaining in an annoyed way? If yes, you have found the meaning.
explain: Querulous is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a voice, a man or a child. «A tired child gave a querulous whine: "Why is it always my turn?"» Here querulous tells you how the whine sounds: whiny and annoyed.
fact: Querulous means complaining in a whining, annoyed voice.
fact: Querulous is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as a voice, a person or a child.
fact: «Querulous» is often used in stories to show a character who moans a lot.
fact: Querulous is not the same as cross: cross shows anger, but querulous is about complaining in a whining way.
fact: To check a new word, swap your meaning into the sentence. «The querulous old man grumbled» still makes sense with complaining in an annoyed voice.
exercise: «The querulous old man grumbled that the soup was cold.» What does querulous mean? | *Complaining in an annoyed, whining voice | Very tall | Happy and singing | Quiet and shy
exercise: «The querulous child whined, "Why is it always my turn?"» Which word in the sentence tells you the child is complaining? | always | turn | child | *whined
exercise: Which part of speech is querulous? | *Adjective | Noun | Verb | Adverb
test: «The querulous customer kept whining that the queue was too long.» What does querulous tell the reader about the customer? | Asleep and dreaming | The customer is lost in the shop | The customer is singing a song | *The customer complains a lot in an annoyed voice
test: Jayden says querulous means the same as cross. What is the best reply? | It means happy and excited | *Not quite: querulous is about a whining, complaining voice, not just anger | It means quiet and calm | It means exactly the same as cross, so there is no difference
exam: After a long day, a querulous voice says, «Why is the tea always cold?» What kind of voice is it? | *Whining and annoyed | Cheerful and loud | Silly and playful | Calm and quiet
